    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0325" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1233.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-18T22:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dominican Government again in peril by General Receiver stopping the five
                    thousand dollars daily advance. No payment for two days. I am apprehensive of
                    trouble unless the Provisional Government is helped out in some way within
                    twenty-four hours. Dominican Government can not get money here and the army
                    restless to the revolting point. Banco Nacional offers to advance money for from
                    thirty to sixty days without interest if the Department will either have public
                    works money on deposit here to cover loan or placed to bank’s credit in New York
                    City. This is the only plan I have heard suggested. Please instruct by wire at
                    once. Of course Government can not live without funds. Quick action absolutely
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
